,"scoringPlay":true,"scoreValue":1,"awayScore":1,"homeScore":0,"text":"Quinn Hughes Goal (5) Snap Shot, assists: Jonas Brodin (5), Nico Sturm (2)","type":{"id":"505","text":"Goal","abbreviation":"goal"},"clock":{"displayValue":"3:42"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"30"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"4320548","displayName":"Quinn Hughes","shortName":"Q. Hughes"},"type":"scorer"},{"athlete":{"id":"2562600","displayName":"Jonas Brodin","shortName":"J. Brodin"},"type":"assister"},{"athlete":{"id":"4320625","displayName":"Nico Sturm","shortName":"N. Sturm"},"type":"assister"}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"1823","guid":"6ae0ec9b-ec2f-35f3-a3c8-98b1076a9623","fullName":"Capital One Arena","address":{"city":"Washington","state":"DC","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1823.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":17393,"officials":[{"fullName":"Riley Brace","displayName":"Riley Brace","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Peter MacDougall","displayName":"Peter MacDougall","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Jonathan Deschamps","displayName":"Jonathan Deschamps","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"CJ Murray","displayName":"CJ Murray","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"2 early goals lift Minnesota to a 5-1 win over Washington, snapping the Capitals' 3-game run","description":"— Quinn Hughes and Michael McCarron scored in the first 5:27 for Minnesota, and the Wild held on for a 5-1 victory over the Washington Capitals on Sunday.","story":"WASHINGTON -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4320548/quinn-hughes\">Quinn Hughes</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3042048/michael-mccarron\">Michael McCarron</a> scored in the first 5:27 for Minnesota, and the Wild held on for a 5-1 victory over the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/wsh/washington-capitals\">Washington Capitals</a> on Sunday.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697783/justin-sourdif\">Justin Sourdif</a> scored the only goal for Washington in the dying seconds of the second period, but the Capitals' three-game winning streak came to an end during this visit by the Central Division-leading Wild.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5302535/maxim-shabanov\">Maxim Shabanov</a>'s power-play goal with 2:23 left in the third restored a two-goal margin, and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3942335/kirill-kaprizov\">Kirill Kaprizov</a> added an empty-netter for his 500th career point and league-leading 15th goal of the season.\n\n\r\n              With 24.9 seconds left and the goalie back in, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5080172/danila-yurov\">Danila Yurov</a> scored one more for Minnesota.\n\n\r\n              Washington had scored at least four goals in five of its previous six games, but the Capitals ran into a stingy Minnesota team and goalie <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4874737/jesper-wallstedt\">Jesper Wallstedt</a>. The Wild permitted two goals or fewer for the fifth time in six games.\n\n\r\n              Minnesota has points in eight of its last nine.\n\n\r\n              Hughes opened the scoring after only 3:42 with his fifth goal of the season. McCarron's shot from the slot made it 2-0.\n\n\r\n              Sourdif deflected the puck past Wallstedt to cut the lead in half.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3101/alex-ovechkin\">Alex Ovechkin</a> has just one goal in his first 13 games in what he's said will be his final NHL season. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5216918/cole-hutson\">Cole Hutson</a> found him on the doorstep with a pass early in the third period, but with the net open, the puck bounced off Ovechkin's skate and he wasn't able to control it.\n\n\r\n              Ovechkin later had a shot from the slot denied by Wallstedt. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3114766/alex-tuch\">Alex Tuch</a> stole the puck near the Minnesota net but was stopped by Wallstedt as well.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4062251/jordan-kyrou\">Jordan Kyrou</a> had a six-game point streak snapped for Washington.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Wild: At Philadelphia on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              Capitals: Host Dallas on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-01T23:21:55Z"}}